{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You were brought in because you were feeling confused and weak. Can you tell me how you're feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m okay now. I was just tired. They gave me something for pain this morning—oxycodone. I think that made me sleepy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. You also had a short dialysis session yesterday. That, along with the pain medicine and a high level of digoxin in your blood, may have contributed to your confusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Digoxin? I take that for my heart. But at the rehab, they were giving it every day, not every other day like at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s likely why your level was high—2.7, which is above the safe range. We’ve held the digoxin for now and will restart it at home on the every-other-day schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So that could’ve made me confused?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially with your kidney function. Your kidneys clear digoxin slowly, so it builds up. We’ll check it again before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve been having more shoulder pain too. That’s why they gave me extra oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. But strong painkillers can make confusion worse, especially when combined with other things. We’re switching to acetaminophen and lidocaine patches to manage your pain more safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to be in pain, but I don’t want to be out of it either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll balance it. Palliative care will help us keep your pain under control without sedation. You’ll keep your morning OxyContin and use low-dose oxycodone as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did a CT scan of your head to make sure there was no stroke or bleeding. It came back normal—no acute issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray showed mild fluid in the lungs, which we think is from missing part of your dialysis. We’ll get you dialyzed tomorrow to clear that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel short of breath though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes it builds up slowly. Your body gets used to it. Dialysis will help remove the extra fluid and improve your breathing, even if you don’t feel it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. When will I get dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow at noon. We’ve scheduled it. Your potassium was high—5.5—which also improves with dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-06-09 19:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time I missed dialysis, my potassium was high too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-06-09 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and this time, it went up to 6, but we caught it early. No heart rhythm issues, so that’s good. Dialysis will bring it down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-06-09 20:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll make sure not to miss dialysis again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are looking better. Your potassium is now 4.4, and creatinine dropped from 6.4 to 4.2 after dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very good. Your mental clarity has improved too. You’re more alert today. The digoxin level is now 2.0—still a bit high but coming down. We’ll restart it at home every other day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heart? I’ve been feeling a little flutter sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw some atrial flutter on the monitor, but your heart rate stayed low—around 50—likely due to the high digoxin. Now that it’s improving, we expect your rhythm to stabilize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m not on blood thinners because of past bleeding, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. Because of your history of GI bleeds, we avoid Coumadin. But we’ll keep you on diltiazem to control your heart rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my calcium? I saw it was high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your calcium is elevated—11.2. Your PTH level was high too, which suggests hyperparathyroidism. We’re starting cinacalcet to help control it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that related to my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. With ESRD, the parathyroid glands can become overactive. Cinacalcet helps lower PTH and calcium. We’ll monitor it over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my shoulder pain—should I get an X-ray?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You already had one as an outpatient. It showed arthritis, no fracture. We’ll keep managing it with lidocaine patches and acetaminophen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been sad lately. It’s the anniversary of my brother’s passing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry to hear that. You’re on citalopram and nortriptyline, which help with both mood and nerve pain. We held mirtazapine for now because it can cause drowsiness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-06-10 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. I just want to feel clear and stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today to the extended care facility. Your mental status is much improved, labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. What do I need to watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take your digoxin every other day—never daily. Watch for nausea, dizziness, or vision changes, which could mean it’s too high. Keep using your pain meds as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay on schedule. Any missed session can lead to fluid or potassium buildup. Also, avoid Fleet enemas—they contain phosphate, which your kidneys can’t handle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll remember that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your follow-up includes seeing neurology for weakness and palliative care for pain. Keep taking cinacalcet daily for your calcium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad you’re feeling clearer. The team will get your discharge papers ready, and you’ll be on your way soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure the rehab staff knows about the digoxin schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please do. We’ve also sent clear instructions to them. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2151-06-11 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-06-09 19:35:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-06-11 15:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis, type 2 diabetes, atrial fibrillation, and a history of steal syndrome was admitted due to altered mental status and weakness after receiving an incomplete dialysis session and excess oxycodone. He was found to have a supratherapeutic digoxin level, likely due to daily administration at his rehab facility instead of every other day. His confusion improved after holding digoxin and narcotics, and completing hemodialysis. Hyperkalemia and mild pulmonary edema resolved with dialysis. Hypercalcemia was detected, and PTH was elevated, leading to the diagnosis of hyperparathyroidism and initiation of cinacalcet. Atrial flutter was observed but remained asymptomatic. Pain management was optimized with acetaminophen, lidocaine patches, and low-dose oxycodone to avoid sedation. He was discharged to extended care with stable mental status, clear instructions on digoxin dosing, and follow-up plans for pain, neurology, and palliative care.",
    "problems": [
      "Toxic encephalopathy",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Major depressive affective disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Hyperparathyroidism, unspecified",
      "Pain in joint, shoulder region",
      "Atrial flutter"
    ]
  }
}
